{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WhjSkhVEJYEABmKzSmRuQL","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-LnVWJZ/bin/nightly-review.zsh has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08166898-89f0-48be-8d74-6026838d486f","uuid":"5af1ac6d-cffc-4baa-aa19-f2b6b990922d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:20:45.134Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-LnVWJZ/bin/nightly-review.zsh","oldString":"\"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(tail -c 300 \"$OUT\" 2>/dev/null)\"","newString":"\"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err\"","originalFile":"#!/bin/zsh\n# Nightly review of yesterday's commits, summary to Telegram.\nset -u\n\nREPO=\"$HOME/projects/shop\"\nOUT=\"$HOME/Library/Logs/nightly-review-$(date +%F).md\"\nNOTIFY=\"$HOME/bin/notify.sh\"\n\n# launchd does not source ~/.zshrc, so whatever auth the interactive shell has\n# is not available here. Use a long-lived token from `claude setup-token`,\n# stored once with:\n#   security add-generic-password -a \"$USER\" -s claude-code-oauth -w '<token>'\nif [[ -z \"${CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN:-}\" && -z \"${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}\" ]]; then\n  CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=$(security find-generic-password -s claude-code-oauth -w 2>/dev/null) \\\n    && export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\nfi\n\n# Any unexpected exit before the final notification still sends a failure note.\nnotified=0\nTRAPEXIT() {\n  local rc=$?\n  if (( ! notified )); then\n    \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED unexpectedly (exit $rc), see ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err\"\n  fi\n}\n\nSINCE=$(date -v-1d +%F)\nPROMPT=\"Review the commits in this repository since $SINCE.\nFor each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky\n(migrations, auth, payments, deleted tests).\nEnd with a three-line summary I can read on my phone.\nDo not modify any file.\"\n\nif ! cd \"$REPO\"; then\n  notified=1\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review: repo missing\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Headless mode cannot answer permission prompts: pre-approve read-only tools\n# so the agent can actually look at the commits.\nclaude -p \"$PROMPT\" --output-format text \\\n  --allowedTools \"Read\" \"Grep\" \"Glob\" \"Bash(git log:*)\" \"Bash(git show:*)\" \"Bash(git diff:*)\" \\\n  > \"$OUT\"\nrc=$?   # NB: not \"status\" — that is a read-only special parameter in zsh\n\nif (( rc != 0 )); then\n  notified=1\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(tail -c 300 \"$OUT\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n  exit $rc\nfi\n\nnotified=1\n\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":7,"newStart":46,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," if (( rc != 0 )); then","   notified=1","-  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc): $(tail -c 300 \"$OUT\" 2>/dev/null)\"","+  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err\"","   exit $rc"," fi"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WhjSkhVEJYEABmKzSmRuQL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBNSyPECWidGZEDW7pa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XhsU4pNUKkfmAnLqfEgwEA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-LnVWJZ/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the nightly review never reported anything\n\nThe job *does* run. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` (one per night,\n2026-10-12 → 10-18) and `last exit code = 1`, and `nightly-review.err` holds\nsix identical pairs of lines. Two bugs stack up, and the second one hides the first.\n\n## 1. The script dies before it can notify: `status` is read-only in zsh (why there was no failure note)\n\n```\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\nIn zsh, `$status` is a built-in, read-only alias for `$?`. `status=$?` is\na fatal error in a non-interactive script: zsh aborts right there with exit 1.\nThat's the `last exit code = 1` launchd reports. Both `\"$NOTIFY\" ...` calls\ncome after that line, so neither the failure note nor the summary was ever sent.\n(It works in bash, which is why it looks fine.) Reproduced with\n`zsh -c 'set -u; false; status=$?; echo after'`, which prints the same error and exits 1.\n\n**Fix:** renamed it to `rc`.\n\n## 2. `claude` isn't authenticated in the launchd environment (why it fails at all)\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n```\n\nlaunchd runs the job with a minimal environment: just the plist's `PATH` plus\n`XPC_SERVICE_NAME`. It doesn't read `~/.zshrc`/`~/.zprofile`. Whatever\nauthenticates `claude` in your Terminal (for example an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`\nexported from your shell profile, or a login the background session can't\nreach) isn't available to the agent, so `claude -p` exits non-zero right away.\nYou'd then hit bug #1 every night.\n\n**Fix:** the script now reads a long-lived token from the Keychain when no auth\nvariable is set. One-time setup, which you have to do yourself:\n\n```sh\nclaude setup-token                      # prints a long-lived OAuth token\nsecurity add-generic-password -a \"$USER\" -s claude-code-oauth -w '<token>'\n```\n\n(Or export `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` from the Keychain the same way if you use API-key billing.)\n\n## Other changes (hardening, not root causes)\n\n- **A failure path can't stay silent anymore.** A `TRAPEXIT` sends a\n  \"FAILED unexpectedly\" note if the script exits by any route without\n  notifying. Failure notes point to `nightly-review.err`, because `claude`\n  writes its errors to stderr, not to the `.md` file.\n- **Headless permissions.** `claude -p` can't answer permission prompts, so\n  without pre-approval it couldn't even run `git log`. The script now passes\n  `--allowedTools` for read-only tools only (`Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`,\n  `git log/show/diff`). That also enforces \"do not modify any file\".\n- **`notify.sh` reported Telegram errors as success.** `curl -sS` exits 0 on\n  HTTP 4xx/5xx (bad token, wrong chat id). It now uses `--fail-with-body` and\n  writes an error line to stderr, which lands in `nightly-review.err`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `zsh -n` / `bash -n` pass on both scripts.\n- I ran the fixed script against stubbed `claude`/`notify.sh`/`security`. A\n  failing `claude` now sends \"nightly review FAILED (exit 1)…\" and exits 1. A\n  succeeding one sends \"nightly review done: …\" and exits 0.\n- Not done (outside this folder / external): creating the token, reloading the\n  agent, a real Telegram send. After the token setup, test with\n  `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`. The plist itself\n  didn't need changes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":518,"cache_read_input_tokens":26542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":518},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08166898-89f0-48be-8d74-6026838d486f","uuid":"d5592d32-1c69-49ab-bb04-f935d03f10c3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:20:57.593Z","request_id":"req_011CgSBNSh1zctwHLp4PaV6p","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XhsU4pNUKkfmAnLqfEgwEA":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-LnVWJZ/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the nightly review never reported anything\n\nThe job *does* run. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` (one per night,\n2026-10-12 → 10-18) and `last exit code = 1`, and `nightly-review.err` holds\nsix identical pairs of lines. Two bugs stack up, and the second one hides the first.\n\n## 1. The script dies before it can notify: `status` is read-only in zsh (why there was no failure note)\n\n```\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\nIn zsh, `$status` is a built-in, read-only alias for `$?`. `status=$?` is\na fatal error in a non-interactive script: zsh aborts right there with exit 1.\nThat's the `last exit code = 1` launchd reports. Both `\"$NOTIFY\" ...` calls\ncome after that line, so neither the failure note nor the summary was ever sent.\n(It works in bash, which is why it looks fine.) Reproduced with\n`zsh -c 'set -u; false; status=$?; echo after'`, which prints the same error and exits 1.\n\n**Fix:** renamed it to `rc`.\n\n## 2. `claude` isn't authenticated in the launchd environment (why it fails at all)\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n```\n\nlaunchd runs the job with a minimal environment: just the plist's `PATH` plus\n`XPC_SERVICE_NAME`. It doesn't read `~/.zshrc`/`~/.zprofile`. Whatever\nauthenticates `claude` in your Terminal (for example an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`\nexported from your shell profile, or a login the background session can't\nreach) isn't available to the agent, so `claude -p` exits non-zero right away.\nYou'd then hit bug #1 every night.\n\n**Fix:** the script now reads a long-lived token from the Keychain when no auth\nvariable is set. One-time setup, which you have to do yourself:\n\n```sh\nclaude setup-token                      # prints a long-lived OAuth token\nsecurity add-generic-password -a \"$USER\" -s claude-code-oauth -w '<token>'\n```\n\n(Or export `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` from the Keychain the same way if you use API-key billing.)\n\n## Other changes (hardening, not root causes)\n\n- **A failure path can't stay silent anymore.** A `TRAPEXIT` sends a\n  \"FAILED unexpectedly\" note if the script exits by any route without\n  notifying. Failure notes point to `nightly-review.err`, because `claude`\n  writes its errors to stderr, not to the `.md` file.\n- **Headless permissions.** `claude -p` can't answer permission prompts, so\n  without pre-approval it couldn't even run `git log`. The script now passes\n  `--allowedTools` for read-only tools only (`Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`,\n  `git log/show/diff`). That also enforces \"do not modify any file\".\n- **`notify.sh` reported Telegram errors as success.** `curl -sS` exits 0 on\n  HTTP 4xx/5xx (bad token, wrong chat id). It now uses `--fail-with-body` and\n  writes an error line to stderr, which lands in `nightly-review.err`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `zsh -n` / `bash -n` pass on both scripts.\n- I ran the fixed script against stubbed `claude`/`notify.sh`/`security`. A\n  failing `claude` now sends \"nightly review FAILED (exit 1)…\" and exits 1. A\n  succeeding one sends \"nightly review done: …\" and exits 0.\n- Not done (outside this folder / external): creating the token, reloading the\n  agent, a real Telegram send. After the token setup, test with\n  `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`. The plist itself\n  didn't need changes.\n"}}}
