{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBPWsK7sy5JsNCZsEUc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night, but two bugs stacked so nothing ever reached Telegram: `claude` fails, and then the script crashes before it can send a failure note. `launchctl print` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, and `nightly-review.err` has the same two errors six times. I've fixed both and written the causes up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing has run for real yet: I only checked syntax and tested the fixed script with stand-ins for `claude`, the notifier and the Keychain.\n\n**Why you got nothing:**\n1. **Why there was no failure note:** `status=$?` is fatal in zsh. In zsh, `status` is a read-only built-in that means the same as `$?`, so assigning to it makes the script stop on line 19 with exit 1. Both notify calls come after that line, so neither one ever ran. (The same line works in bash, which is why it looks fine.) I reproduced the exact error. **Fix:** renamed the variable to `rc`.\n2. **Why `claude` fails:** it isn't logged in when launchd runs it (\"Not logged in · Please run /login\"). launchd starts the job with a bare environment and doesn't read your shell profile, so whatever logs `claude` in from your Terminal isn't there. **Fix:** the script now reads a long-lived token from the Keychain.\n\n**One step you have to do yourself**, since it's outside this folder:\n```sh\nclaude setup-token\nsecurity add-generic-password -a \"$USER\" -s claude-code-oauth -w '<token>'\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review   # run once now to test\n```\n\n**Smaller fixes so failures can't go quiet again:**\n- **Catch-all failure note:** if the script exits any other way without notifying, it now sends a \"FAILED unexpectedly\" message.\n- **Read-only permissions for `claude`:** it runs without anyone to approve actions, so it couldn't even run `git log`. The script now pre-approves read-only tools only (reading files and `git log`/`show`/`diff`), which also enforces \"do not modify any file\".\n- **Telegram errors are no longer silent:** `notify.sh` used to exit as if it had succeeded when Telegram rejected the message (for example a bad token or chat id). It now reports the failure to `nightly-review.err`.\n\nThe plist didn't need any changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1742,"cache_read_input_tokens":27060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1742},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08166898-89f0-48be-8d74-6026838d486f","uuid":"468cf6f5-e926-4afb-ba11-a3428aeedde2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:21:05.609Z","request_id":"req_011CgSBPWch2GKLzsSZcTAxf"}
